flowchart TD
    Doctrine[Autopsy Doctrine\nEvidence-first operator assessment]
    Canon[Canonical Directives\nLocked principles + governance rules]
    Architecture[Architecture Layer\nSystem design + boundary control]
    Core[Core Product\nIndustry-agnostic operating platform]
    Sleeve[Industry Sleeves\nVertical domain logic]
    Cleaning[Cleaning Sleeve\nFirst vertical]
    Autopsy[Autopsy\nPre-business diagnostic gate]
    Operator[Operator / Client\nEvidence, decisions, behaviour]

    Supabase[Supabase\nCanonical truth + validation]
    N8N[n8n\nOrchestration + telemetry]
    Notion[Notion\nManagement + visibility]
    GitHub[GitHub\nVersion control + rollback]
    Codex[Codex\nRepo execution assistant]
    Mermaid[Mermaid\nArchitecture diagrams]
    EOD[EOD Master Index\nDaily authority record]
    SOD[SOD Directive\nNext-day execution brief]

    Doctrine --> Canon
    Canon --> Architecture
    Architecture --> Core
    Core --> Sleeve
    Sleeve --> Cleaning
    Autopsy --> Operator
    Operator --> Autopsy
    Autopsy --> Core
    Autopsy -. gates readiness for .-> Sleeve

    GitHub --> Canon
    GitHub --> Architecture
    GitHub --> Mermaid
    Codex --> GitHub
    Mermaid --> Architecture

    Supabase --> Core
    Supabase --> Autopsy
    Supabase --> N8N
    N8N --> Supabase
    N8N --> Notion
    Notion --> Operator

    N8N --> EOD
    EOD --> SOD
    SOD --> Operator
    EOD --> GitHub
    SOD --> GitHub

    Canon -. prevents drift .-> Core
    Architecture -. protects Core boundary .-> Sleeve
    Supabase -. source of truth .-> Notion
    Notion -. not canonical .-> Supabase
    GitHub -. rollback authority .-> Supabase
    N8N -. logged controlled mutation .-> Supabase

    classDef governance fill:#f5f5f5,stroke:#333,stroke-width:1px;
    class Doctrine,Canon,Architecture,EOD,SOD governance;
